# Release signing. The key and its passwords never enter the repository: the
# signing identity is what proves an update came from us, and a key in git is
# a key everyone has. CI supplies these from secrets; keep your own backup
# somewhere durable, because losing it means no existing install can ever be
# updated again.
*.jks
*.keystore
/keystore.properties

